acy of fidarestat, a novel aldose reductase inhibitor, for diabetic peripheral neuropathy: a 52-week multicenter placebo-controlled double-blind parallel group study</article-title><source>Diabetes Care</source><year>2001</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>1776</fpage><lpage>1782</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11574441</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b6"><label>6</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hotta</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Yasuda</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Sumita</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Sano</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kakuta</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Nagashima</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Effects of a novel aldose reductase inhibitor, fidarestat (SNK-860), on vibration perception threshold and subjective symptoms in patients with diabetic polyneuropathy: An open-label pilot study</article-title><source>Clin Drug Invest</source><year>2004</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>671</fpage><lpage>680</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b7"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bril</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Buchanan</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><collab>the AS-3201 Study Group</collab></person-group><article-title>Aldose reductase inhibition by AS-3201 in sural nerve from patients with diabetic sensorimotor polyneuropathy</article-title><source>Diabetes Care</source><year>2004</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>2369</fpage><lpage>2375</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15451902</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bril</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Bucha